    default n
    help
        Enable Service Registration Protocol Client
        Disable to save ~20KB

endmenu # Security Features

menu "Radio Configuration"

config OPENTHREAD_RADIO_COEX_ENABLE
    bool "Enable Radio Coexistence"
    default n
    help
        Enable coexistence with other radios (BLE, WiFi)

config OT_HEARTBEAT_MS
    int "OpenThread task safety-net heartbeat (ms, 0 = none)"
    range 0 600000
    default 1500
    help
        The OpenThread task wakes on every event; the heartbeat only bounds
        a missed notification.  Each heartbeat is an RTOS deadline that ends
        a deep-sleep window: low-power builds use a long one (e.g. 30000).

config IPRO_PM_THREAD
    bool "Platform PDS between radio activity (ipro_pm)"
    default n
    depends on IPRO_PM && IEEE802154_ENABLE && !THREAD_RADIO_SPINEL
    select IPRO_PM_IDLE_PDS
    help
        Register the 802.15.4 radio with ipro_pm: the idle task enters
        PDS31 while the radio has nothing to do (a SED between data polls,
        an SSED between CSL sample windows), sized to the next microsecond
        alarm; the MAC configuration is written back after the SoC reset
        of the PDS and the RF is warmed up again.  A device with its
        receiver on while idle (MED, router) stays at WFI.  Replaces
        CONFIG_THREAD_LP_SLEEP.  With BLE connected PDS (IPRO_PM_PDS_CONNECTED)
        the controller runs the PDS and the radio sleeps in it.
        Raw per-app .config builds must also set CONFIG_IPRO_PM_IDLE_PDS=y
        and CONFIG_IPRO_PM_TIMEBASE=y.

config IPRO_PM_THREAD_WAKE_LEAD_US
    int "CPU back before the microsecond alarm (us)"
    default 1000
    depends on IPRO_PM_THREAD

config IPRO_PM_THREAD_RF_RESTORE
    bool "Warm the RF up after a PDS that powered it down"
    default y
    depends on IPRO_PM_THREAD

config IPRO_PM_THREAD_ALIGN
    bool "Line Thread's periodic radio work up with the BLE link (experimental)"
    default n
    depends on IPRO_PM_THREAD
    help
      With a BLE link in the PDS profile the controller runs one PDS per
      connection interval; a Thread deadline in the middle of it cuts that
      PDS short and the rest of the interval is spent at WFI.  An SSED
      gets its CSL period set to an integer fraction of the connection
      interval and its sample phase moved to just after the connection
      event (the parent learns it from the data poll that follows); the
      application's period comes back when the link goes.

      Measured worse than leaving it alone (2026-09-28, SSED CSL 1 s, BLE
      1005 ms): 30-36 % PDS unaligned, 0-8 % aligned.  The window has no
      room before the anchor (the controller spends the time after its
      wake on the restore) and a PDS entry the controller is granted a
      few ms after the event is refused or released.  It needs the
      controller to publish a fresh window after an early wake (more than
      one PDS per interval).

config IPRO_PM_THREAD_ALIGN_SED
    bool "Also move a SED's data polls onto BLE wakes"
    default n
    depends on IPRO_PM_THREAD_ALIGN
    help
      Poll at every k-th BLE wake (k = round(poll period / interval)),
      OpenThread's own poll timer pushed half an interval later as the
      fallback.  Measured worse than OpenThread's own schedule (SED 1 s
      poll, BLE 1005 ms: 34-37 % vs 71-75 % PDS), so off.

config OPENTHREAD_MAC_CSL_RECEIVER_ENABLE
    bool "Enable CSL Receiver"
    default n
    help
        Enable Coordinated Sampled Listening (requires microsecond timer)

endmenu # Radio Configuration

